item.description:
arXiv:2511.00137v3 Announce Type: replace Abstract: We consider an integral transform given by $T_{
u} f(s) := \pi \int_0^\infty rs J_{
u}(r s)^2 f(r) \, dr$, where $J_{
u}$ denotes the Bessel function of the first kind of order $
u$. As shown by Walther (2002, doi:10.1006/jfan.2001.3863), this transform plays an essential role in the study of optimal constants of smoothing estimates for the free Schr"{o}dinger equation on $\mathbb{R}^d$. On the other hand, Bez et al. (2015, doi:10.1016/j.aim.2015.08.025) studied these optimal constants using a different method, and obtained a certain alternative expression for $T_{
u} f$ involving the $d$-dimensional Fourier transform of $x \mapsto f(\lvert x vert)$ when $
u = k + d/2 - 1$ for $k \in \mathbb{N}$. In this paper, we extend their identity to non-integer indices and derive several inequalities from it. In particular, we give a dimension-comparison result for the smoothing estimates on $\mathbb{R}^d$ and $\mathbb{R}^{d+1}$.
